help.loop family:
Read --instances (zeno-fcis/loop-family-manifest/1) and --program (zeno-fcis/loop-expressions/1 with $PARAMETERS). Parameter values belong in the manifest; the family program must not supply its own. Files and named canonical programs are at most 65,536 bytes; the manifest lists 1 to 10 instances with relative paths and signed-64-bit JSON integer parameter values. Each instance is limited to 131,072 input tuples.

Lower or solve the program per instance, then require transform check plus matching receipt replay. --fit proposes affine hole values a*$P+b from instances marked for fitting and checks the lifted program on all listed instances. This establishes no unlisted-instance claim. No session or attempts; per-instance reports include receipt digests, not exported receipt files.

JSON: zeno-fcis/loop-doors/2. Exit 0 accepted summarizes the initial per-instance checks; the fitted template has a separate detail.lifted_check verdict, which does not change that exit. Exit 1 refuted or invalid input; 2 unrealizable/partial or containment inconclusive; 3 I/O error.

Usage: zeno-fcis loop family [OPTIONS] --instances <INSTANCES> --program <PROGRAM>

Options:
      --containment-backend <CONTAINMENT_BACKEND>
          Backend override; otherwise ZENO_FCIS_CONTAINMENT_BACKEND, then auto (finite data only)

          [possible values: auto, systemd, posix]

      --instances <INSTANCES>
          Instance manifest (zeno-fcis/loop-family-manifest/1)

      --kb <KB>
          Ordered external KB files; omission consults ZENO_FCIS_KB for loop sessions

      --program <PROGRAM>
          Family program (zeno-fcis/loop-expressions/1) over $PARAMETERS

      --fit
          Fit each hole's values to a * $P + b and check the lifted program

      --no-kb
          Disable automatic KB consultation, including stored session configuration

      --kb-task <KB_TASK>
          Explicit task/size/environment facts for automatic loop advice

          [default: ""]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')


Engine: Per-instance expression lowering or bounded sketch/repair proposes; every successful instance requires transform check and matching receipt replay.
Contract: ["stdout zeno-fcis/loop-doors/2, door=family, authority=none: detail rows with programs/check/replay digests and coverage of the listed instances. No receipt files, session or attempts are exported.","Where integer_encoding is present, scalar report integers use safe-number-or-decimal-string/1. Program JSON bounds/literals remain decimal strings; node references remain JSON integers."]
