help.loop transfer:
Read --from (zeno-fcis/loop-expressions/1 with source parameters) and --to-instances (zeno-fcis/loop-family-manifest/1). Source parameter values are signed-64-bit JSON integers. Source expressions must be plain and use literal constants, not $PARAMETERS. Use the supplied source parameter values to locate constants near changed target parameters; try direct use, open those constants as choice holes, then try repair. Every successful target program needs transform check and matching receipt replay on that target reference domain.

At most 10 listed instances, 131,072 tuples per instance, and 65,536 bytes per document/program; bounded search/check stages share the invocation deadline. No session or attempts; report receipt digests without exporting receipt files. Coverage is only the listed instances.

JSON: zeno-fcis/loop-doors/2. Exit 0 transferred to all; 1 failed (none) or refused; 2 partial or containment inconclusive. Per-target budget stops can aggregate to failed (1) or partial (2); inspect rows; 3 I/O error.

Usage: zeno-fcis loop transfer [OPTIONS] --from <FROM> --to-instances <TO_INSTANCES>

Options:
      --containment-backend <CONTAINMENT_BACKEND>
          Backend override; otherwise ZENO_FCIS_CONTAINMENT_BACKEND, then auto (finite data only)

          [possible values: auto, systemd, posix]

      --from <FROM>
          Source program (zeno-fcis/loop-expressions/1) with its instance's parameters

      --kb <KB>
          Ordered external KB files; omission consults ZENO_FCIS_KB for loop sessions

      --to-instances <TO_INSTANCES>
          Target instance manifest (zeno-fcis/loop-family-manifest/1)

      --no-kb
          Disable automatic KB consultation, including stored session configuration

